From 0d41769574faea294a57831631318a820e53a48d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 18:04:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Azure port management, custom login, reimage, prices and
 region flags

Extends the Azure VM epic to match the UpCloud feature set more closely,
per user request to make Azure "work exactly like the website" for the
things UpCloud already covers:

- Port/firewall management: list, add and delete inbound NSG security
  rules per VM (mirrors the Networking blade in the Azure Portal).
  Priority for new rules is auto-assigned above whatever exists.
- VM creation now lets the user type a custom admin username (Azure
  rejects reserved names like root/admin, validated via
  is_valid_azure_username) instead of a fixed "azureuser", and lets them
  either auto-generate a password or type their own (12-72 chars).
- Added OS reimage (Azure's real /reimage action - reinstalls the OS
  from the original image, wiping the disk but keeping name/network/
  size/IP) alongside the existing stop/start/restart/delete actions.
- VM size picker now shows an hourly USD price estimate per size,
  fetched from the public Azure Retail Prices API (best-effort, never
  blocks the picker if pricing is unavailable).
- Region picker now shows a country flag next to each Azure location,
  matching the flag treatment already used for UpCloud zones.

All five additions are covered by fake-server tests in both the
service layer (port rule CRUD incl. priority ordering, reimage,
pricing lookup incl. unknown-SKU fallback, username validation, VM
creation with a custom admin username) and the handler layer (the full
new FSM steps for username/password-mode/custom-password, the ports
list/add/delete flow, reimage confirm+action, and that price/flag
strings actually render in the picker labels). Full UpCloud/Cloud VPS
regression suite re-run clean after these changes.

